_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 27
---
order: 27
---
short_label: III.27
---
statement: In equal circles angles standing on equal circumferences equal one another whether they stand at the centers or at the circumferences.
---
proof:

For in equal circles *ABC* and *DEF,* on equal circumferences *BC* and *EF,* let the angles *BGC* and *EHF* stand at the centers *G* and *H,* and the angles *BAC* and *EDF* at the circumferences.

I say that the angle *BGC* equals the angle *EHF,* and the angle *BAC* equals the angle *EDF.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="470" height="240" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="III.27 diagram" src="propIII27.gif"/></noscript>
